  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Seqlock",
      "source_hash": 11820119200402662176,
      "context_hash": 3019549472381472611,
      "translation": "Seqlock",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "seqlock": "seqlock"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257069Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:0/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Sequence counters for lockless reads of small, frequently-updated data",
      "source_hash": 15163075675819784277,
      "context_hash": 2348536249171001464,
      "translation": "작고 자주 갱신되는 데이터를 락 없이 읽기 위한 시퀀스 카운터",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257070Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "The seqlock pattern",
      "source_hash": 8606038130275674719,
      "context_hash": 3929863015226996933,
      "translation": "seqlock 패턴",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "seqlock": "seqlock"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "A seqlock (sequence lock) solves a specific problem: how do you let readers access small data (like a timestamp or a counter) without taking any lock, while still detecting if a concurrent write happened?",
      "source_hash": 2670775839633844228,
      "context_hash": 2920276472455350869,
      "translation": "seqlock(sequence lock)은 특정한 문제를 해결합니다. 바로 리더가 어떤 락도 잡지 않고 작은 데이터(타임스탬프나 카운터 등)에 접근하면서도, 동시에 쓰기가 일어났는지를 감지할 수 있게 하려면 어떻게 해야 하는가라는 문제입니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "seqlock": "seqlock",
        "timestamp": "타임스탬프"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "The writer increments a sequence counter before and after writing.",
      "source_hash": 6656974120122811430,
      "context_hash": 18047308480621585979,
      "translation": "라이터는 쓰기 전과 후에 시퀀스 카운터를 증가시킵니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "A reader reads the counter before and after reading the data.",
      "source_hash": 6452562544329221987,
      "context_hash": 11181301302306770455,
      "translation": "리더는 데이터를 읽기 전과 후에 카운터를 읽습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:2/seg:2",
      "source": "If the counter changed (or is odd, meaning a write is in progress), the reader retries:",
      "source_hash": 15711323261602753330,
      "context_hash": 14785998936147849470,
      "translation": "카운터가 바뀌었거나 홀수이면(쓰기가 진행 중이라는 뜻입니다) 리더는 재시도합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:1/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "This gives **zero-cost reads when there are no concurrent writes**, and cheap retries otherwise.",
      "source_hash": 12283663729074842844,
      "context_hash": 13208055208175888933,
      "translation": "이를 통해 **동시 쓰기가 없을 때는 비용이 전혀 들지 않는 읽기**를 얻을 수 있으며, 그렇지 않은 경우에도 재시도 비용이 저렴합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Two types: seqcount_t and seqlock_t",
      "source_hash": 11471017781619590069,
      "context_hash": 7836827417546213515,
      "translation": "두 가지 타입: seqcount_t와 seqlock_t",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:2/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "`seqlock_t` is the complete package for most users. `seqcount_t` is used when the writer serialization is handled by some other mechanism (e.g., a mutex).",
      "source_hash": 11932835468448702752,
      "context_hash": 550642384983120348,
      "translation": "`seqlock_t`는 대부분의 사용자를 위한 완전한 패키지입니다. `seqcount_t`는 라이터 직렬화를 다른 메커니즘(예: 뮤텍스)이 처리할 때 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "mutex": "뮤텍스"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257071Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "API",
      "source_hash": 17306549135961116108,
      "context_hash": 7447655961742257110,
      "translation": "API",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "API": "API"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "seqlock_t",
      "source_hash": 13419891067439217381,
      "context_hash": 4207834893532844252,
      "translation": "seqlock_t",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:3/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "seqcount_t",
      "source_hash": 8989861926840747875,
      "context_hash": 11964642175300594490,
      "translation": "seqcount_t",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Real-world example: jiffies and time",
      "source_hash": 17352912841292786383,
      "context_hash": 3114504708047440899,
      "translation": "실제 사례: jiffies와 시간",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "jiffies": "jiffies"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "The kernel uses seqlocks extensively for time-related data that is updated on every timer tick but read from many places:",
      "source_hash": 4986076652319186869,
      "context_hash": 7106746669053623737,
      "translation": "커널은 타이머 틱마다 갱신되지만 여러 곳에서 읽히는 시간 관련 데이터에 seqlock을 광범위하게 사용합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "kernel": "커널",
        "seqlocks": "seqlock",
        "timer": "타이머"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:4/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "The `jiffies_64` counter is also protected by a seqlock on 32-bit systems (where a 64-bit read is non-atomic):",
      "source_hash": 9405820052995892265,
      "context_hash": 18442496232342905239,
      "translation": "`jiffies_64` 카운터 역시 32비트 시스템(64비트 읽기가 원자적이지 않은 환경)에서는 seqlock으로 보호됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "bit": "비트",
        "seqlock": "seqlock"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Constraints",
      "source_hash": 11930884711566436492,
      "context_hash": 7130574354426951983,
      "translation": "제약 사항",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Seqlocks have important limitations:",
      "source_hash": 8690616158134910936,
      "context_hash": 8607574056016542714,
      "translation": "seqlock에는 중요한 제약이 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "seqlocks": "seqlock"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "**No pointers**: readers cannot follow pointers during the critical section.",
      "source_hash": 10652734670431911339,
      "context_hash": 6105499014337056013,
      "translation": "**포인터 사용 불가**: 리더는 임계 구역 안에서 포인터를 따라갈 수 없습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "critical section": "임계 구역"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:2/seg:1",
      "source": "If the writer frees the old object between the reader's pointer dereference and its use, the reader has a dangling pointer.",
      "source_hash": 12732304808955463978,
      "context_hash": 15147556099649287015,
      "translation": "리더가 포인터를 역참조한 시점과 그것을 사용하는 시점 사이에 라이터가 이전 객체를 해제하면, 리더는 댕글링 포인터(dangling pointer)를 갖게 됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:2/seg:2",
      "source": "Use RCU instead for pointer-based data.",
      "source_hash": 13331350012940521738,
      "context_hash": 10912991352438458377,
      "translation": "포인터 기반 데이터에는 대신 RCU를 사용하십시오.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "RCU": "RCU"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257072Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:0",
      "source": "**Small, bounded data**: the retry loop must be cheap and terminating.",
      "source_hash": 5323328787274044306,
      "context_hash": 8331841177032219362,
      "translation": "**작고 크기가 제한된 데이터**: 재시도 루프는 비용이 저렴하고 반드시 종료되어야 합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:3/seg:1",
      "source": "Don't protect megabytes of data or data with variable-length reads.",
      "source_hash": 8022994913385967422,
      "context_hash": 1700012156562829241,
      "translation": "메가바이트 단위의 데이터나 가변 길이로 읽는 데이터를 보호하지 마십시오.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:4/seg:0",
      "source": "**Writer progress**: writes complete quickly.",
      "source_hash": 15602649692797074971,
      "context_hash": 12117921539996629118,
      "translation": "**라이터 진행**: 쓰기는 빠르게 완료되어야 합니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:4/seg:1",
      "source": "If writes are frequent or long, readers will spin in the retry loop.",
      "source_hash": 5682906970323943293,
      "context_hash": 14693462685735154744,
      "translation": "쓰기가 잦거나 길면 리더는 재시도 루프에서 계속 돌게 됩니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:5/block:5/seg:0",
      "source": "**No blocking in reader**: the reader critical section must not sleep (the data could change while asleep).",
      "source_hash": 7491811118265857550,
      "context_hash": 13324655168005448677,
      "translation": "**리더에서 블로킹 금지**: 리더 임계 구역에서는 슬립해서는 안 됩니다(슬립하는 동안 데이터가 바뀔 수 있기 때문입니다).",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "critical section": "임계 구역"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:0/seg:0",
      "source": "Seqlock vs rwlock",
      "source_hash": 17476373919029336849,
      "context_hash": 226393552474619548,
      "translation": "Seqlock 대 rwlock",
      "glossary_snapshot": {
        "seqlock": "seqlock"
      },
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:1/seg:0",
      "source": "Both allow concurrent readers, but:",
      "source_hash": 1390688665160501317,
      "context_hash": 1790468351169621342,
      "translation": "둘 다 동시 리더를 허용하지만 다음과 같은 차이가 있습니다.",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
      "issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "section:6/block:2/seg:0",
      "source": "rwlock",
      "source_hash": 655047487294012947,
      "context_hash": 5496096553352378900,
      "translation": "rwlock",
      "glossary_snapshot": {},
      "translated_at": "2026-11-14T22:16:05.257073Z",
